<title>JAPAN: Japan Jan pork imports rise 56.5 pct yr/yr -- MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan Jan pork imports rise 56.5 pct yr/yr -- MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's pork imports in January rose by 56.5 percent to 33,997 tonnes from a year earlier, Finance Ministry data showed on Friday.</p>
<p>Details were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		     Jan 97	Dec 96	 Jan 96</p>
<p> Total	     33,997	43,552	 21,722</p>
<p> Refrigerated     9,258	11,605	 13,262</p>
<p> Frozen	    24,739	31,947	  8,460</p>
<p>Major suppliers of refrigerated pork (in tonnes):</p>
<p> Taiwan	     4,167	 5,392	  3,482</p>
<p> U.S.		 4,234	 5,366	  4,497</p>
<p>Major supplier of frozen pork (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		     Jan 97	Dec 96	 Jan 96</p>
<p> Taiwan	    11,838	24,182	  8,750</p>
<p>Imports of refrigerated pork in calendar 1996 totalled 168,859 tonnes, up 0.9 percent from 167,392 tonnes in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>Imports of frozen pork in calendar 1996 totalled 484,274 tonnes, up 17.2 percent from 413,144 tonnes in 1995, ministry data showed.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-7431</p>
</text>
